<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Verona</h1><p class="st-meta">1262 CE – 1387 CE · capital Verona</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Scaliger lordship that made Verona a power in north-eastern Italy, whose lord Cangrande della Scala sheltered Dante.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezzelino-iii-da-romano">Ezzelino III da Romano</a> died in 1259, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Commune of Verona</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastino-i-della-scala">Mastino I della Scala</a> as its leader, and by 1262 he was effectively lord. His family, the della Scala or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaligeri</a>, made the office hereditary.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaligeri</a> ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> as lords and imperial vicars. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cangrande-i-della-scala">Cangrande I</a>, lord from 1311 to 1329, conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-vicenza">Vicenza</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-treviso">Treviso</a> and hosted the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, who dedicated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paradiso-dante">Paradiso</a> to him. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mastino-ii-della-scala">Mastino II</a> the lordship reached <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-lucca">Lucca</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-parma">Parma</a>, but a coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-florence">Florence</a> stripped most of it away in 1339. The family's Gothic tombs, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger-tombs">Arche Scaligere</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castelvecchio-verona">Castelvecchio</a> bridge survive.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Family murders weakened the dynasty. In 1387 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a> seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a> from Antonio della Scala and annexed it to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> took the city in 1405.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-verona.jpg" alt="Lordship of Verona" width="320" height="374"><figcaption>Image: Xander · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stemma_della_Scala.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1262 CE – 1387 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Verona</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mastino I della Scala, Cangrande I della Scala, Mastino II della Scala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Venetian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Scaliger lordship, Della Scala</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1324&amp;focus=lordship-of-verona" aria-label="Lordship of Verona on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4941 575 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Verona lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5261 831L5261 831M5261 831L5218 830M5261 831L5293 831M5261 831L5274 828"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5261 831h0M5218 830h0M5293 831h0M5274 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5261 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5261 831h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Verona. <a href="/atlas?year=1324&amp;focus=lordship-of-verona">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
